screen.SUN=Sun & Moon
screen.LIGHTS=Local Lights
screen.LIGHT_SHADOWS=Local Light Shadows
screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
profile.LOW=Low
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.HIGH=High
profile.ULTRA=Ultra
option.SUN_STRENGTH=Sunlight Strength
option.SUN_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the directional sun. Higher = stronger, darker-contrast shadows.
option.MOON_STRENGTH=Moonlight Strength
option.MOON_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the directional moon at night (also shadow casting). Varies with moon phase.
option.AMBIENT_DAY=Daytime Ambient
option.AMBIENT_DAY.comment=Brightness of shadowed areas in daylight. Lower = deeper shadows.
option.SUN_SHADOW_QUALITY=Sun Shadow Filtering
option.SUN_SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=Number of shadow samples. Higher = smoother shadow edges.
option.SUN_SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Sun Shadow Softness
option.SUN_SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of sun/moon shadow edges.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Path Tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilts the sun's path so noon shadows are not straight down.
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Shadow map size. Higher = sharper shadows from fences, leaves and entities, but slower.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from the player sun/moon shadows are drawn (blocks).
option.LIGHT_INTENSITY=Light Intensity
option.LIGHT_INTENSITY.comment=Brightness of torches, lanterns, lava, portals and other block lights.
option.LIGHT_RANGE=Light Range
option.LIGHT_RANGE.comment=Scales how far each light reaches (1.00 = about the vanilla light level in blocks).
option.COLOR_STRENGTH=Color Strength
option.COLOR_STRENGTH.comment=0 = every light is vanilla warm. 1 = each light uses its own colour (soul fire blue, portals purple, froglights...).
option.VANILLA_FILL=Light Spread
option.VANILLA_FILL.comment=Soft, coloured fill that follows Minecraft's own light spreading around corners and through doors.
option.DAY_SUPPRESS=Daylight Suppression
option.DAY_SUPPRESS.comment=Reduces local light under open sky by day. Never affects night or caves.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Local Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=0 = razor sharp torch shadows. Higher = softer penumbra (uses temporal smoothing).
option.SHADOW_RAY_STEPS=Local Shadow Ray Steps
option.SHADOW_RAY_STEPS.comment=Maximum half-block steps a torch-shadow ray walks. Lower is faster but long rays may leak light.
option.MAX_LIGHTS_PER_PIXEL=Lights Per Pixel
option.MAX_LIGHTS_PER_PIXEL.comment=Strongest N local lights ray-traced for every pixel. Main performance control for lights.
option.DEBUG_VIEW=Debug View
option.DEBUG_VIEW.comment=1 lights-per-cell heat map, 2 lighting only, 3 voxelisation check (surfaces green), 4 status panel (6 squares, all green when working), 5 G-buffer mask (green = ok), 6 sun/moon shadow only.
option.LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS=Fine Light Shadows
option.LIGHT_SS_SHADOWS.comment=Experimental: trace torchlight through the depth buffer so players, mobs and dropped items cast a shadow. The depth buffer only holds the nearest surface, so objects between you and the lit ground (fences, the lamp itself) can cast a phantom shadow across it. Off by default.
option.LIGHT_SS_COUNT=Fine Shadow Lights
option.LIGHT_SS_COUNT.comment=How many of the strongest nearby lights use the precise ray. Lower is cheaper.
option.LIGHT_SS_STEPS=Fine Shadow Steps
option.LIGHT_SS_STEPS.comment=Length of the precise light ray. Higher reaches further at a small cost.
